>Or popping out of a sink or fountain. (Or out of a lamp. Or summoned
>by a god. Or by an angry guard or shopkeeper. Or racing in from nowhere
>to deliver mail. Or randomly generated on the current level. Or budded
>off of an existing pudding or gremlin.)

Hey...

* Sewer rats and black puddings come from the pipes under the sink.
* Water elementals come out of the faucet.
* Water moccasins, nymphs and water demons come from the (underwater)
source of the fountain.
* Randomly generated monsters are assumed to appear by trapdoors or
level teleport magic from "behind the curtain" (i.e other levels).
* Magic lamps, divine minions, Keystone Kops and vault guards all use
magic.
* Mail daemons are daemons in the Neal Stephenson sense - they can
break the rules of the software because they are a part of the
software.
* Monster fission is not "created from nothing".

Meanwhile:

* Fishing hooks can pull fish (a monster) out a space that, if you
actually plunge into the water, contains nothing.

The point I'm getting at is:
* As long as the monster comes from an unseen & inaccessible location
that is assumed to be reachable from the terrain square, then it's
fine. Empty water doesn't fullfil that criterion.

Also:
* I don't see why, if you can fish with a pole, you shouldn't be
allowed to dive in and grab the fish with your bare hands (or polymorph
into a shark if that doesn't work)



